course: dictionary
lesson: 10318
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Track» can mean a running course, a set of rails, a mark left on the ground, or a song. To find the right meaning, read the context: the words around it give the clues.
explain: «Outside, the fresh tracks in the mud lead straight to the Wild Wood.» Mud and fresh show that tracks are marks left on the ground, probably footprints. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: «Electric trains take their power from overhead wires or from a third rail beside the track.» Trains run on rails, so here track means the metal rails. Always check the other words in the sentence, not just the one you don't know.
explain: To track something means to follow its marks or where it goes. To keep track of something means to know where it is or to keep count of it, as in «you keep track of how much you have».
fact: A track can be a path or course for running, the metal rails that trains run on, a mark left by a person or animal, or one song on an album.
fact: To track means to follow the marks of something, or to follow where it goes.
fact: To keep track of something is to keep count of it or know where it is.
fact: Never play on railway tracks, because trains are very dangerous.
exercise: «Outside, the fresh tracks in the mud lead straight to the Wild Wood.» What are the tracks? | Metal rails for trains | A song on an album | *Marks left on the ground by feet or paws | A running course for races
exercise: Maya runs laps on the school running track. What is a running track? | The metal rails trains run on | *A path or course for running or racing | Marks left in the mud by an animal | One song on an album
exercise: Pocket money tip: «you keep track of how much you have». What does keep track mean here? | Give it away to a friend | Lose it on purpose | Put it in a safe place and forget it | *Know how much you have, or keep count
test: Rangers can track a wolf by following its footprints. What does track mean in this sentence? | To pull a train along rails | To play a song loudly | *To follow the marks of something | To run a race round a course
test: Sam runs 5 laps of the track, and each lap is 400 metres. Which word means the path he runs on? | Keep | *Track | Rails | A song
exam: Which sentence uses track to mean one piece of music on an album? | The train waited on the track | You must keep track of your homework | *The third track on the album is my favourite | We saw tracks of a fox in the snow
